# KnockOut — Sports analyzed

A free, line-by-line analyzer for NFL, MLB, NBA and NHL games.

```
knockout/
├── website/   # Plain HTML/CSS/JS website
└── app/       # iPhone + Android app (React Native / Expo)
```

Both share the same pages, translations (English, German, Spanish, French) and demo game data.

| Page | Website | App |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Home | `index.html` | Home tab |
| Sign in | `signin.html` | Sign In screen |
| Analytics | `analytics.html` | Analytics tab |
| Who We Are | `about.html` | Who We Are tab |
| Privacy Policy & User Agreement | `privacy.html` | Privacy tab |

## Website

No build step. Open `website/index.html` in a browser, or serve the folder:

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000 --directory website
```

Then go to http://localhost:8000. The `website` folder can be uploaded as-is to any static host (GitHub Pages, Netlify, Vercel).

## App

Needs [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) (LTS).

```bash
cd app
npm install
npx expo install --fix
npx expo start
```

Scan the QR code with the **Expo Go** app on your phone to open KnockOut. Building for the App Store or Google Play is done with [EAS Build](https://docs.expo.dev/build/introduction/).

## Before launch

These parts are demo stand-ins:

- **Game data** — `website/js/data.js` and `app/src/data.js` hold sample games. Swap in a live sports data API.
- **Sign in** — Google, Apple and email sign-in only save a name on the device. Connect a real auth provider (Firebase Auth, Supabase, Auth0, or Google Identity Services + Sign in with Apple).
- **Chatbot** — rule-based answers from a glossary. For full AI answers, call an AI model from your own backend.
- **Who We Are** — fill in the CMO and CFO names and bios.
- **Privacy Policy** — template text; add your contact email and have it reviewed by a lawyer.
